{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Now I understand the \"their example\" — Scene 1: BoomBox PBR (a glTF model + environment + arc-rotate camera). The user wants to turn this into a Quake-style FPS with destructible terrain.\n\nWorking directory: `/private/tmp/.../scratchpad/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps` — empty. This is the project to build. It's named \"babylon-lite-minecraft-fps\" but the request is Quake-style FPS with destructible terrain. Either way, I'll build it in this working directory.\n\nPlan:\n1. Create a Vite project in the working directory, using `babylon-lite` from the local reference repo (pnpm workspace link). The reference repo is at ~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite, and the package `babylon-lite` is at packages/babylon-lite, whose main points to `./src/index.ts`. So we can link it as a workspace dependency.\n\nLet me check the structure of the reference repo: pnpm-workspace.yaml, packages/babylon-lite (main: ./src/index.ts, sideEffects: false). So the dependency `babylon-lite: link:~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite/packages/babylon-lite` will work in pnpm.\n\nImportant: GUIDANCE.md says the lab is a dev playground. I'll create a standalone Vite app in the working directory:\n\n- package.json with babylon-lite as a workspace/link dependency\n- vite.config.ts\n- index.html with a canvas\n- src/main.ts: FPS game\n\nGame requirements (Quake-style FPS with destructible terrain):\n- First-person camera: pointer lock, WASD, mouse look, jump, gravity\n- Weapon: click to fire, raycast hit detection\n- Destructible terrain: heightmap terrain mesh; when a projectile hits, remove/lower vertices near the hit point (crater) and rebuild the mesh. For a Quake-style look, use chunked voxels or a heightfield with craters.\n\nSimplest and most robust approach: heightfield terrain (e.g., 256x256 grid, chunked into 16x16 or 32x32 chunks). Store heights in a Float32Array. When hit at (x,z), carve a crater: lower heights within a radius with a smooth falloff, and rebuild the affected chunk's geometry (positions, normals, indices). This is fast and looks Quake-like (digging tunnels into the ground).\n\nAlso, add some destructible blocks/crates? \"Destructible terrain\" is the requirement. I'll go with heightfield craters + maybe a few destructible boxes that get removed on hit. Focus: terrain craters.\n\nPerformance: 256x256 heightfield with 32x32 chunks → 64 chunks. Crater update: recompute one or a few chunks. Each chunk has (32+1)^2 vertices ≈ 1089 vertices, 32*32*2 = 2048 triangles. No problem.\n\nPhysics: simple character controller on top of the heightfield: sample terrain height at player position, gravity, jump. Also collide with the walls (keep within the map boundary).\n\nWeapon: hitscan (ray from camera along view direction). Ray vs terrain: sample the heightfield along the ray (binary search or step). Simpler: DDA on the heightfield grid? For a heightfield, ray marching in small steps (e.g., 0.1 units) is sufficient for short ranges. Alternatively, use the engine's picking feature! The feature list says \"Ray Casting / Picking ✅ GPU ID pass + CPU ray/triangle details\". The engine has picking functionality. But picking against a terrain mesh with updated geometry — the engine's picking is GPU-based; it should work if I rebuild the mesh geometry. Let me check the picking API in the lite source.\n\nActually, let me check what picking APIs exist in babylon-lite's src. Let me search.\n\nI also need to check how to create a dynamic/custom mesh: there's `mesh` in src. Let me look at the mesh API — createBox, createSphere, etc. For terrain, I probably need a custom mesh with position/normals/indices. Let me check whether there's an API to create a mesh from raw geometry data.\n\nAlso check: FreeCamera for FPS (Scene 18 — WASD controls). The feature list says \"Free Camera ✅ Scene 18, 24, 25 — WASD/arrow controls\". Let me look at scene18 to see how FPS-style controls are done.\n\nAlso, shadows: ESM/PCF available. Fog: available. IBL environment loading available.\n\nLet me explore the relevant APIs:\n1. src/mesh — custom mesh creation from arrays\n2. src/picking — raycast API\n3. src/camera — FreeCamera, attachControl\n4. src/scene — per-frame callbacks (onFrameRender?), update loop hooks\n5. src/light — shadow generators\n6. src/shadow — ESM setup\n\nLet me take a look at scene18 (Free Camera) and scene24/25, and check the index exports.\n","seq":1500,"t":136253,"text":"\n\nLet me look at the engine's API surface to plan the build.\n\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":18944,"draft_n":3430,"draft_n_accepted":841,"predicted_ms":19320.0,"predicted_n":1331,"prompt_ms":2060.0,"prompt_n":2133},"to_request":1039}
