{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Two issues:\n1. pnpm 11 no longer reads the `pnpm` field in package.json — settings have moved to `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. So add `onlyBuiltDependencies: [esbuild]` to pnpm-workspace.yaml.\n2. esbuild can't be required from the project root (pnpm's strict node_modules — esbuild is a transitive dependency of vite, not a direct dependency). That's fine; test via vite instead.\n\nAlso note: the reference repo has a pnpm-workspace.yaml — but my project is standalone; creating a pnpm-workspace.yaml in my own directory is fine (it won't conflict since it's a separate directory).\n\nWait — actually, if I create a pnpm-workspace.yaml in my own directory, pnpm will treat my directory as the workspace root. If I define packages: [packages/*]… no, just put onlyBuiltDependencies in there. Actually, according to pnpm's docs, `onlyBuiltDependencies` in pnpm-workspace.yaml is the new location. Let's create it.\n","seq":9480,"t":679551,"text":"\n\npnpm 11 moved that setting to `pnpm-workspace.yaml`:\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":77312,"draft_n":812,"draft_n_accepted":337,"predicted_ms":6070.0,"predicted_n":453,"prompt_ms":1930.0,"prompt_n":964},"to_request":9400}
