{"kind":"delta","request":11524,"seq":11760,"t":933502,"tool_call":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"const { chromium } = require(\\\"playwright\\\");\\n\\n(async () => {\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n        args: [\\n            \\\"--force-color-profile=srgb\\\",\\n            \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n            \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n            \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n            \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n            \\\"--disable-vulkan-fallback-to-gl-for-testing\\\",\\n            \\\"--ignore-gpu-blocklist\\\",\\n        ],\\n    });\\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n    const errors = [];\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", (msg) => {\\n        if (msg.type() === \\\"error\\\") errors.push(msg.text());\\n    });\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", (err) => errors.push(\\\"PAGEERROR: \\\" + err.message));\\n\\n    await page.goto(\\\"http://localhost:5180/\\\", { waitUntil: \\\"load\\\" });\\n    await page.waitForSelector('canvas[data-ready=\\\"true\\\"]', { timeout: 30000 });\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: \\\"shot1.png\\\" });\\n\\n    // fire 24 shots all around, refilling ammo between bursts\\n    const info = await page.evaluate(async () => {\\n        const q = window.__quake;\\n        let fires = 0;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < 24; i++) {\\n            q.player.yaw = (i / 24) * Math.PI * 2;\\n            q.player.pitch = -0.12;\\n            q.weapon.fireCooldown = 0;\\n            q.weapon.ammo = q.weapon.clipSize;\\n            q.weapon.reloading = false;\\n            if (q.fire()) fires++;\\n            await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 60));\\n        }\\n        return {\\n            fires,\\n            craters: q.weapon.craters,\\n            ammo: q.weapon.ammo,\\n            cratesAlive: q.crates.filter((c) => c.alive).length,\\n            player: [q.player.x.toFixed(1), q.player.y.toFixed(1), q.player.z.toFixed(1)],\\n        };\\n    });\\n    console.log(\\\"SHOTS\\\", JSON.stringify(info));\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(1500);\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: \\\"shot2.png\\\" });\\n\\n    // walk forward for a couple of seconds\\n    await page.keyboard.down(\\\"KeyW\\\");\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\\n    await page.keyboard.up(\\\"KeyW\\\");\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(500);\\n    const pos = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const q = window.__quake;\\n        return [q.player.x.toFixed(1), q.player.y.toFixed(1), q.player.z.toFixed(1)];\\n    });\\n    console.log(\\\"WALKED\\\", JSON.stringify(pos));\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: \\\"shot3.png\\\" });\\n\\n    console.log(\\\"ERRORS\\\", JSON.stringify(errors.slice(0, 10)));\\n    await browser.close();\\n})().catch((e) => {\\n    console.error(\\\"FAIL\\\", e.message);\\n    process.exit(1);\\n});\", \"path\": \"/scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/verify.cjs\"}","id":"call_f6f29f7966554dfc913db1aa","index":0,"name":"write"}}
{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The file is fine (indentation was preserved). Next, I'll write a Playwright verification script using the reference repo's playwright installation. To make `require('playwright')` resolve, I'll run it from the reference repo's directory.\n\nScript:\n```js\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\n\n(async () => {\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({\n    args: [\n      '--force-color-profile=srgb',\n      '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\n      '--enable-features=Vulkan',\n      '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\n      '--use-angle=swiftshader',\n      '--disable-vulkan-fallback-to-gl-for-testing',\n      '--ignore-gpu-blocklist',\n    ],\n  });\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\n  const errors = [];\n  page.on('console', (msg) => { if (msg.type() === 'error') errors.push(msg.text()); });\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push('PAGEERROR: ' + err.message));\n  await page.goto('http://localhost:5180/', { waitUntil: 'load' });\n  await page.waitForSelector('canvas[data-ready=\"true\"]', { timeout: 30000 });\n  await page.waitForTimeout(1500);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'shot1.png' });\n  // Fire 30 shots in various directions\n  const info = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const q = window.__quake;\n    let fires = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) {\n      q.player.yaw = (i / 30) * Math.PI * 2;\n      q.player.pitch = -0.15;\n      if (q.fire()) fires++;\n    }\n    return { fires, craters: q.weapon.craters, ammo: q.weapon.ammo, player: [q.player.x, q.player.y, q.player.z] };\n  });\n  console.log('SHOTS', JSON.stringify(info));\n  await page.waitForTimeout(1500);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'shot2.png' });\n  console.log('ERRORS', JSON.stringify(errors.slice(0, 10)));\n  await browser.close();\n})().catch((e) => { console.error('FAIL', e.message); process.exit(1); });\n```\n\nNote: fire() is limited by fireCooldown (0.11 seconds) — firing 30 times in a single evaluate: tryFire returns false when cooldown > 0. That means only about 1 shot per cooldown... no wait, cooldown is updated in the render loop. Within a single synchronous evaluate, dt isn't advancing, so the cooldown stays at 0.11 → only the first shot gets fired. I need to fire across frames: either loop with small awaits interspersed, or temporarily set weapon.fireCooldown = 0 each time. Let's do this: `q.weapon.fireCooldown = 0; if (q.fire()) fires++;` — but ammo is only 20. After 20 shots, ammo hits 0 → auto-reload begins → subsequent shots won't fire. To test more shots, top up ammo each time: `q.weapon.ammo = q.weapon.clipSize; q.weapon.reloading = false;`.\n\nAlso, the screenshots: I'll save them to the project directory and load them to verify visually.\n\nWhere do I run it from? I'll place the script in the reference repo directory (temporary) — no, better to keep the reference repo clean: use NODE_PATH pointing to the reference repo's node_modules and run the script from my own project directory. NODE_PATH works with CJS require. I'll write the script as .cjs in my own project directory.\n","seq":11761,"t":933502,"text":"\n\nNow a headless verification pass using the reference repo's Playwright + SwiftShader WebGPU:\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":92928,"draft_n":2618,"draft_n_accepted":1333,"predicted_ms":20990.0,"predicted_n":1707,"prompt_ms":1780.0,"prompt_n":690},"to_request":11524}
{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"const { chromium } = require(\\\"playwright\\\");\\n\\n(async () => {\\n    const browser = await chromium.launch({\\n        args: [\\n            \\\"--force-color-profile=srgb\\\",\\n            \\\"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\\\",\\n            \\\"--enable-features=Vulkan\\\",\\n            \\\"--use-vulkan=swiftshader\\\",\\n            \\\"--use-angle=swiftshader\\\",\\n            \\\"--disable-vulkan-fallback-to-gl-for-testing\\\",\\n            \\\"--ignore-gpu-blocklist\\\",\\n        ],\\n    });\\n    const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n    const errors = [];\\n    page.on(\\\"console\\\", (msg) => {\\n        if (msg.type() === \\\"error\\\") errors.push(msg.text());\\n    });\\n    page.on(\\\"pageerror\\\", (err) => errors.push(\\\"PAGEERROR: \\\" + err.message));\\n\\n    await page.goto(\\\"http://localhost:5180/\\\", { waitUntil: \\\"load\\\" });\\n    await page.waitForSelector('canvas[data-ready=\\\"true\\\"]', { timeout: 30000 });\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: \\\"shot1.png\\\" });\\n\\n    // fire 24 shots all around, refilling ammo between bursts\\n    const info = await page.evaluate(async () => {\\n        const q = window.__quake;\\n        let fires = 0;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < 24; i++) {\\n            q.player.yaw = (i / 24) * Math.PI * 2;\\n            q.player.pitch = -0.12;\\n            q.weapon.fireCooldown = 0;\\n            q.weapon.ammo = q.weapon.clipSize;\\n            q.weapon.reloading = false;\\n            if (q.fire()) fires++;\\n            await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 60));\\n        }\\n        return {\\n            fires,\\n            craters: q.weapon.craters,\\n            ammo: q.weapon.ammo,\\n            cratesAlive: q.crates.filter((c) => c.alive).length,\\n            player: [q.player.x.toFixed(1), q.player.y.toFixed(1), q.player.z.toFixed(1)],\\n        };\\n    });\\n    console.log(\\\"SHOTS\\\", JSON.stringify(info));\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(1500);\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: \\\"shot2.png\\\" });\\n\\n    // walk forward for a couple of seconds\\n    await page.keyboard.down(\\\"KeyW\\\");\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\\n    await page.keyboard.up(\\\"KeyW\\\");\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(500);\\n    const pos = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const q = window.__quake;\\n        return [q.player.x.toFixed(1), q.player.y.toFixed(1), q.player.z.toFixed(1)];\\n    });\\n    console.log(\\\"WALKED\\\", JSON.stringify(pos));\\n    await page.screenshot({ path: \\\"shot3.png\\\" });\\n\\n    console.log(\\\"ERRORS\\\", JSON.stringify(errors.slice(0, 10)));\\n    await browser.close();\\n})().catch((e) => {\\n    console.error(\\\"FAIL\\\", e.message);\\n    process.exit(1);\\n});\", \"path\": \"/scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/verify.cjs\"}","id":"call_f6f29f7966554dfc913db1aa","kind":"tool_call","name":"write","outcome":"ran","request":11524,"seq":11762,"shown":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: /scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/verify.cjs.","t":933548,"turn":3}
