th (param \"SECRET_1\"))\n  (subpath (param \"SECRET_2\"))\n  (subpath (param \"SECRET_3\"))\n  (subpath (param \"SECRET_4\"))\n  (subpath (param \"SECRET_5\"))\n  (subpath (param \"SECRET_6\"))\n  (subpath (param \"SECRET_7\"))\n  (subpath (param \"SECRET_8\")))\n(deny file-read* file-write* (require-all (regex #\"/\\.env(\\.[^/]*)?$\") (require-not (regex #\"/\\.env\\.(example|sample|template|dist)$\")) (require-not (subpath (param \"WORKTREE\")))))\n","--","bash","-c","cd ~/git/me/discipline/.claude/worktrees/react-spa-prototype-e65246 && ls diet/ && head -40 diet/AGENTS.md"],"cwd":"/scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps","exit":0,"id":"call_dedc6f092df54e18b6535ff8","isolation":"sandbox","kind":"tool_call","name":"bash","network":"host","outcome":"ran","request":12623,"seq":12655,"shown":"AGENTS.md\nCargo.toml\nREADME.md\nadapters\ncapture\nclient\ndigest\ndogma\ndrive\nformats\nisolation\nseam\nsrc\ntests\nwasm\n# CONTENT\n- Prose for judgment, schema for format, mechanical grounding for truth: Three layers; none substitutes for another. *Specimen: the model \"can't do JSON\" (false), \"can do JSON\" (8/8), and \"does JSON too well\" — 454 plausible API names emitted into a field whose definition invited enumeration; 248 existed nowhere.*\n- Advisory framing for reference material; imperatives only at the cheapest effective site: Imperative injection causes over-pivoting and sycophantic capitulation on false positives; advisory framing preserves the model's ability to decline.\n- One grammar per format, expressed as data, one authorized implementation: Anything else claiming to parse the format passes the shared conformance corpus or it isn't a parser of that format. *Specimen: eleven divergent decline-detection rules across three languages, and \"I recreated it in Python to be quick.\"*\n\n\n# MECHANISMS\n- Fixtures pin what the author was thinking about: Conformance corpora and mutation find what nobody was.\n- Salience needs a prior. A blind extractor has none: Extraction verifies provenance, never meaning.\n- Any lane that writes with capture authority carries a mechanical groundedness gate against its contract input: Schema pressure generates to fill the form. Judgment-class fields (plans, opinions) are exempt — grounding them is a category error.\n- Judgment compiled into data: Do the expensive judgment once, version it, and let cheap machinery apply it. A sense-description is a salience specification authored by a model capable of judgment, executed by a model capable only of distance. *Specimen: an abstract sentence matched concrete transcript prose at cosine 0.82.*\n- Deterministic projections over interpretation chains: No subagent search parties where a purpose-built tool produces receipts at zero entropy. Every summarize-then-interpret hop is a lossy re-encode.\n- One grammar per format under `diet/formats/<name>/`, with `fixtures/valid/` and `fixtures/invalid/` and a `.reason` beside each invalid fixture; the conformance test is the format's definition.\n- The CLI (`diet check-*`, `diet parse-*`) is the only way anything outside this library reads a format; the resolver refuses a stale or planted binary rather than choosing. What this forbids is a foreign reader: a second implementation of the format. `diet/wasm` is not one; it is the same library under a second build target, calling `diet`'s own format functions, conformance-equal to native by #78's gate.\n- The working object: patches are typed, dedup aliases rather than rebinds, a turn is atomic and order-independent (the permutation test), and the regimen is immutable for the session.\n\n\n# GRADING\n- Protocols amend by versioned bump, never in place: Vendor advice is input to the next version, not an override of the current one.\n- Measured, not computed: Memory, cache, costs — measure. *Specimen: the ecosystem's own KV-cache arithmetic for a model family was wrong by 4×.*\n- Any speculative or optimization path used in graded runs demonstrates output-invariance first: A throughput gain that changes outputs is a regime change wearing an optimization's clothes. *Specimen: a patched drafter selector raised decode speed and induced chain-of-thought loops; the acceptance math no longer described the proposer.*\n- Truncated output is a typed outcome: A capped generation is never graded as wrong or malformed.\n\n\n# ROLES\n- Small models classify and disambiguate. They never trigger or generate on the authority path: Determinism first: lexical anchors, then embeddings, then a constrained verdict — and classical reconciliation merges the results.\n- Judge seats are calibrated on hand-authored controls before trust, and judge prompts are pinned as instruments: *Specimen: one model scored at chance on controls it should have found easy; another scored 19/19 — the difference was capability, not ambiguity, and the calibration lived only in a session transcript until it was pinned.*\n","stderr":"","stderr_bytes":0,"stdout":"AGENTS.md\nCargo.toml\nREADME.md\nadapters\ncapture\nclient\ndigest\ndogma\ndrive\nformats\nisolation\nseam\nsrc\ntests\nwasm\n# CONTENT\n- Prose for judgment, schema for format, mechanical grounding for truth: Three layers; none substitutes for another. *Specimen: the model \"can't do JSON\" (false), \"can do JSON\" (8/8), and \"does JSON too well\" — 454 plausible API names emitted into a field whose definition invited enumeration; 248 existed nowhere.*\n- Advisory framing for reference material; imperatives only at the cheapest effective site: Imperative injection causes over-pivoting and sycophantic capitulation on false positives; advisory framing preserves the model's ability to decline.\n- One grammar per format, expressed as data, one authorized implementation: Anything else claiming to parse the format passes the shared conformance corpus or it isn't a parser of that format. *Specimen: eleven divergent decline-detection rules across three languages, and \"I recreated it in Python to be quick.\"*\n\n\n# MECHANISMS\n- Fixtures pin what the author was thinking about: Conformance corpora and mutation find what nobody was.\n- Salience needs a prior. A blind extractor has none: Extraction verifies provenance, never meaning.\n- Any lane that writes with capture authority carries a mechanical groundedness gate against its contract input: Schema pressure generates to fill the form. Judgment-class fields (plans, opinions) are exempt — grounding them is a category error.\n- Judgment compiled into data: Do the expensive judgment once, version it, and let cheap machinery apply it. A sense-description is a salience specification authored by a model capable of judgment, executed by a model capable only of distance. *Specimen: an abstract sentence matched concrete transcript prose at cosine 0.82.*\n- Deterministic projections over interpretation chains: No subagent search parties where a purpose-built tool produces receipts at zero entropy. Every summarize-then-interpret hop is a lossy re-encode.\n- One grammar per format under `diet/formats/<name>/`, with `fixtures/valid/` and `fixtures/invalid/` and a `.reason` beside each invalid fixture; the conformance test is the format's definition.\n- The CLI (`diet check-*`, `diet parse-*`) is the only way anything outside this library reads a format; the resolver refuses a stale or planted binary rather than choosing. What this forbids is a foreign reader: a second implementation of the format. `diet/wasm` is not one; it is the same library under a second build target, calling `diet`'s own format functions, conformance-equal to native by #78's gate.\n- The working object: patches are typed, dedup aliases rather than rebinds, a turn is atomic and order-independent (the permutation test), and the regimen is immutable for the session.\n\n\n# GRADING\n- Protocols amend by versioned bump, never in place: Vendor advice is input to the next version, not an override of the current one.\n- Measured, not computed: Memory, cache, costs — measure. *Specimen: the ecosystem's own KV-cache arithmetic for a model family was wrong by 4×.*\n- Any speculative or optimization path used in graded runs demonstrates output-invariance first: A throughput gain that changes outputs is a regime change wearing an optimization's clothes. *Specimen: a patched drafter selector raised decode speed and induced chain-of-thought loops; the acceptance math no longer described the proposer.*\n- Truncated output is a typed outcome: A capped generation is never graded as wrong or malformed.\n\n\n# ROLES\n- Small models classify and disambiguate. They never trigger or generate on the authority path: Determinism first: lexical anchors, then embeddings, then a constrained verdict — and classical reconciliation merges the results.\n- Judge seats are calibrated on hand-authored controls before trust, and judge prompts are pinned as instruments: *Specimen: one model scored at chance on controls it should have found easy; another scored 19/19 — the difference was capability, not ambiguity, and the calibration lived only in a session transcript until it was pinned.*\n","stdout_bytes":4095,"t":7930611,"turn":4}
