E + height/2...). Keep the bot's feet at ground level: body center y = ground + 0.8.\n- Behavior:\n  - Wander: pick a random point within the arena (avoiding rim mountains? just within radius 40); walk toward it at walk speed; re-pick on arrival or on a timer.\n  - Combat: if player is within 30 units and has LOS (raycast from bot's eye to player's eye returns null → clear), aim at player (with slight error), fire every 0.5–1.2s (random). Bot shots: hitscan — first check player hit (ray vs player sphere: distance from ray to player position < 0.5), then terrain, then crates. On player hit: damage (10–20).\n  - Bot vs bot? Keep it simple: bots only target the player.\n- Bot death: when health <= 0 → removed from scene, respawn after 5s at a random spawn point. Player can destroy bots (aim ray vs bot AABB before terrain).\n- Player: health 100, HUD display; on death → respawn at (0, ground, 0), 2s invulnerability, health reset.\n- Bots carve craters when shooting terrain (they shoot the terrain too) — makes the arena lively.\n\n**Player damage**: add to weapon.ts or a new combat module. Bot hit on player: ray from bot's eye to player; player is a sphere of radius 0.5 centered on eye (close enough).\n\n**Player hit on bot**: in tryFire, before terrain: check each bot's AABB (body box). If bot hit → damage bot (30), if <=0 → death (remove mesh, mark dead, respawn timer).\n\n**LOS check**: terrain.raycast(botEye → playerEye dir, dist) — if hit is closer than player distance → no LOS. Crates also block LOS (rayAabb) — nice detail, include it.\n\n**Bots shoot crates too** — same fire path.\n\nFrame loop: onBeforeRender → updateBots(bots, player, terrain, crates, dt, onPlayerHit callback).\n\nStructure for multiplayer later: keep all sim state in plain objects (players: Player[], bots: Bot[]), and keep update functions pure-ish (mutate state, no DOM). HUD is a separate render step. I'll note this in the README.\n\nAlso update the README in the project directory (per the repo's AGENTS.md convention: docs are written anew, rules placed where they're read). The project needs a README.md — write it in the worktree... no, in the scratchpad project directory.\n\nNow let's write bots.ts.\n\nDetails:\n- BOT_SPEED = 8\n- Bot eye height = 1.5\n- Body: box size 0.9 (x,z), height 1.6 → createBox(engine, 1) scaled to (0.9, 1.6, 0.9), center at feet+0.8\n- Head: box 0.55, at feet+1.85\n- Color: different diffuse per bot (e.g., [0.8,0.2,0.2], [0.2,0.8,0.3], [0.3,0.4,0.9], [0.9,0.7,0.2])\n- Damage: player → bot: 34 (3 shots to kill, 100hp). Bot → player: 8–14 per hit.\n- Bot fire cooldown: random 0.6–1.4s.\n- Bot aim: target = player eye + small random offset (error ~1.5 units at 20 range) → recompute direction each frame while in combat; fire when cooldown expires.\n- Bot movement: simple: face the movement direction (yaw = atan2(dx, dz)); if in combat, face the player instead.\n- Bot ground: same snap as player (sampleHeight + eye height).\n- Bots don't jump; walk through craters (craters are 2.8 deep, 7 wide — a bot walking over the edge would suddenly snap down; acceptable).\n- Avoid map rim: keep target within radius 40 from origin.\n\nRespawn: bot.dead=true, deadTimer; after 5s, reset position to a random spawn point (ring of radius 20–35), health 100, re-add mesh (setMeshVisible? or removeFromScene/addToScene). Simplest: keep the mesh in the scene, and use `setMeshVisible(mesh, false)` when dead — exported! `setMeshVisible` is in index.ts ✓. And remove from the shadow casters? Trivial — leaving it as a caster while invisible... the shadow task will render invisible casters? setSubtreeVisible exists; setMeshVisible probably marks the renderable as skipped. Shadows might still draw it. Simplest and most robust: removeFromScene on death, addToScene on respawn, and re-call setShadowTaskCasterMeshes with alive bots + crates.\n\nPlayer death: overlay \"YOU DIED — RESPAWNING\"; invulnerability 2s; bots stop targeting during invulnerability.\n\nHUD: add HEALTH bar/text.\n\nLet's also update the debug handle (__quake) to include bots.\n\nNow let's write the code.\n","seq":13857,"t":8073665,"text":"\n\nThe worktree root is outside my writable sandbox (EPERM on mkdir), so the project stays where the harness mirrors it — continuing here. Implementing the scope now: noise terrain is done, adding **bots** (and player health/respawn to make them meaningful), with the sim kept in plain data so multiplayer can slot in later.\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":105984,"draft_n":8799,"draft_n_accepted":3141,"predicted_ms":73930.0,"predicted_n":4398,"prompt_ms":2330.0,"prompt_n":939},"to_request":13131}
{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"import {\\n    addToScene,\\n    createBox,\\n    createStandardMaterial,\\n    removeFromScene,\\n    setMeshVisible,\\n    type EngineContext,\\n    type Mesh,\\n    type SceneContext,\\n} from \\\"babylon-lite\\\";\\nimport type { Terrain } from \\\"./terrain\\\";\\nimport type { Player } from \\\"./player\\\";\\nimport type { Crate } from \\\"./weapon\\\";\\nimport { rayAabb } from \\\"./weapon\\\";\\n\\nexport interface Bot {\\n    x: number;\\n    y: number; // eye height, world\\n    z: number;\\n    yaw: number;\\n    health: number;\\n    maxHealth: number;\\n    dead: boolean;\\n    respawnTimer: number;\\n    wanderX: number;\\n    wanderZ: number;\\n    fireCooldown: number;\\n    body: Mesh;\\n    head: Mesh;\\n}\\n\\nexport const BOT_EYE = 1.5;\\nconst BOT_SPEED = 8;\\nconst BOT_RADIUS = 40; // stay inside this radius from origin\\nconst RESPAWN_TIME = 5;\\nconst WANDER_RADIUS = 38;\\n\\nconst BOT_COLORS: [number, number, number][] = [\\n    [0.8, 0.25, 0.2],\\n    [0.25, 0.75, 0.3],\\n    [0.3, 0.45, 0.9],\\n    [0.9, 0.7, 0.2],\\n];\\n\\nfunction randRange(a: number, b: number): number {\\n    return a + Math.random() * (b - a);\\n}\\n\\nfunction pickWanderPoint(b: Bot): void {\\n    const ang = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;\\n    const r = Math.sqrt(Math.random()) * WANDER_RADIUS;\\n    b.wanderX = Math.cos(ang) * r;\\n    b.wanderZ = Math.sin(ang) * r;\\n}\\n\\nexport function spawnBots(engine: EngineContext, scene: SceneContext, terrain: Terrain, count: number): Bot[] {\\n    const bots: Bot[] = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\\n        const color = BOT_COLORS[i % BOT_COLORS.length]!;\\n        const body = createBox(engine, 1);\\n        body.scaling.set(0.9, 1.6, 0.9);\\n        const bodyMat = createStandardMaterial();\\n        bodyMat.diffuseColor = color;\\n        bodyMat.specularColor = [0.1, 0.1, 0.1];\\n        body.material = bodyMat;\\n        const head = createBox(engine, 1);\\n        head.scaling.set(0.55, 0.55, 0.55);\\n        const headMat = createStandardMaterial();\\n        headMat.diffuseColor = [Math.min(1, color[0] + 0.15), Math.min(1, color[1] + 0.15), Math.min(1, color[2] + 0.15)];\\n        headMat.specularColor = [0.1, 0.1, 0.1];\\n        head.material = headMat;\\n\\n        const bot: Bot = {\\n            x: 0,\\n            y: 0,\\n            z: 0,\\n            yaw: 0,\\n            health: 100,\\n            maxHealth: 100,\\n            dead: false,\\n            respawnTimer: 0,\\n            wanderX: 0,\\n            wanderZ: 0,\\n            fireCooldown: randRange(0.5, 1.5),\\n            body,\\n            head,\\n        };\\n        respawnBot(bot, terrain, i);\\n        addToScene(scene, body);\\n        addToScene(scene, head);\\n        bots.push(bot);\\n    }\\n    return bots;\\n}\\n\\n/** (Re)place a bot at a random spawn ring. Does not touch scene membership. */\\nexport function respawnBot(b: Bot, terrain: Terrain, index: number): void {\\n    const ang = (index / 4) * Math.PI * 2 + Math.random() * 0.8;\\n    const r = randRange(18, 32);\\n    b.x = Math.cos(ang) * r;\\n    b.z = Math.sin(ang) * r;\\n    b.y = terrain.sampleHeight(b.x, b.z) + BOT_EYE;\\n    b.health = b.maxHealth;\\n    b.dead = false;\\n    b.fireCooldown = randRange(0.5, 1.5);\\n    pickWanderPoint(b);\\n    syncBotMeshes(b);\\n}\\n\\nfunction syncBotMeshes(b: Bot): void {\\n    b.body.position.set(b.x, b.y - BOT_EYE + 0.8, b.z);\\n    b.head.position.set(b.x, b.y - BOT_EYE + 1.9, b.z);\\n}\\n\\n/** Does the bot have line of sight to the player? (terrain + crates block) */\\nfunction hasLOS(b: Bot, p: Player, terrain: Terrain, crates: Crate[]): boolean {\\n    const dx = p.x - b.x;\\n    const dy = p.y - b.y;\\n    const dz = p.z - b.z;\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dy, dz);\\n    if (dist < 0.001) return true;\\n    const nx = dx / dist;\\n    const ny = dy / dist;\\n    const nz = dz / dist;\\n    for (const c of crates) {\\n        if (!c.alive) continue;\\n        const t = rayAabb(b.x, b.y, b.z, nx, ny, nz, c.mesh.position.x, c.mesh.position.y, c.mesh.position.z, c.size / 2);\\n        if (t !== null && t < dist) return false;\\n    }\\n    const hit = terrain.raycast(b.x, b.y, b.z, nx, ny, nz, dist);\\n    return hit === null || hit.dist >= dist - 0.5;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Step all bots. `onPlayerHit(damage)` is called when a bot shot lands on the player.\\n * Returns the damage dealt to the player this frame (0 if none).\\n */\\nexport function updateBots(\\n    bots: Bot[],\\n    player: Player,\\n    playerInvulnerable: boolean,\\n    terrain: Terrain,\\n    crates: Crate[],\\n    scene: SceneContext,\\n    dt: number,\\n    onPlayerHit: (damage: number) => void\\n): void {\\n    for (const b of bots) {\\n        if (b.dead) {\\n            b.respawnTimer -= dt;\\n            if (b.respawnTimer <= 0) {\\n                respawnBot(b, terrain, bots.indexOf(b));\\n                addToScene(scene, b.body);\\n                addToScene(scene, b.head);\\n            }\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n\\n        const dx = player.x - b.x;\\n        const dy = player.y - b.y;\\n        const dz = player.z - b.z;\\n        const distToPlayer = Math.hypot(dx, dy, dz);\\n        const canSee = !playerInvulnerable && distToPlayer < 30 && hasLOS(b, player, terrain, crates);\\n\\n        if (canSee) {\\n            // face and shoot the player\\n            b.yaw = Math.atan2(dx, dz);\\n            b.fireCooldown -= dt;\\n            if (b.fireCooldown <= 0) {\\n                b.fireCooldown = randRange(0.6, 1.4);\\n                // aim with error, scaled by distance\\n                const err = distToPlayer * 0.06;\\n                const tx = player.x + randRange(-err, err);\\n                const ty = player.y + randRange(-err, err);\\n                const tz = player.z + randRange(-err, err);\\n                const adx = tx - b.x;\\n                const ady = ty - b.y;\\n                const adz = tz - b.z;\\n                const alen = Math.hypot(adx, ady, adz);\\n                const nx = adx / alen;\\n                const ny = ady / alen;\\n                const nz = adz / alen;\\n                // player hit? (eye sphere, radius 0.5)\\n                const cx = b.x - player.x;\\n                const cy = b.y - player.y;\\n                const cz = b.z - player.z;\\n                const tca = cx * nx + cy * ny + cz * nz;\\n                const d2 = cx * cx + cy * cy + cz * cz - tca * tca;\\n                if (tca > 0 && d2 < 0.25) {\\n                    onPlayerHit(Math.round(randRange(8, 14)));\\n                } else {\\n                    // miss the player: carve terrain / break crates\\n                    let blocked = Infinity;\\n                    for (const c of crates) {\\n                        if (!c.alive) continue;\\n                        const t = rayAabb(b.x, b.y, b.z, nx, ny, nz, c.mesh.position.x, c.mesh.position.y, c.mesh.position.z, c.size / 2);\\n                        if (t !== null && t < blocked) blocked = t;\\n                    }\\n                    const hit = terrain.raycast(b.x, b.y, b.z, nx, ny, nz, 120);\\n                    if (hit !== null && hit.dist < blocked) {\\n                        terrain.carveCrater(hit.point[0], hit.point[2], 3.0, 2.2);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n            }\\n        } else {\\n            // wander\\n            const wx = b.wanderX - b.x;\\n            const wz = b.wanderZ - b.z;\\n            const wd = Math.hypot(wx, wz);\\n            if (wd < 1.5) {\\n                pickWanderPoint(b);\\n            } else {\\n                b.yaw = Math.atan2(wx, wz);\\n                b.x += (wx / wd) * BOT_SPEED * dt;\\n                b.z += (wz / wd) * BOT_SPEED * dt;\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        // ground snap\\n        b.y = terrain.sampleHeight(b.x, b.z) + BOT_EYE;\\n        syncBotMeshes(b);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n/** AABB of a bot's body + head, world space. */\\nexport function botAabb(b: Bot): { cx: number; cy: number; cz: number; hx: number; hy: number; hz: number } {\\n    return {\\n        cx: b.x,\\n        cy: b.y - BOT_EYE + 1.1, // midpoint between body center and head\\n        cz: b.z,\\n        hx: 0.5,\\n        hy: 1.3,\\n        hz: 0.5,\\n    };\\n}\\n\\nexport function killBot(b: Bot, scene: SceneContext): void {\\n    b.dead = true;\\n    b.respawnTimer = RESPAWN_TIME;\\n    setMeshVisible(b.body, false);\\n    setMeshVisible(b.head, false);\\n    removeFromScene(scene, b.body);\\n    removeFromScene(scene, b.head);\\n}\", \"path\": \"/scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/src/bots.ts\"}","id":"call_c75c6774488049f79e4acf50","kind":"tool_call","name":"write","outcome":"ran","request":13131,"seq":13858,"shown":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: /scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/src/bots.ts.","t":8073714,"turn":4}
