{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"OK, let's verify with `vite build` (which compiles the entire module graph — catches import/type resolution errors). Run tsc too? tsc will check the linked package's TS — heavy but skipLibCheck helps. Actually `vite build` doesn't type-check. For type errors, run `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` — but that will type-check the entire babylon-lite source (huge, may have its own issues under my tsconfig). My tsconfig only includes \"src\" — tsc will still pull in babylon-lite types via imports. With skipLibCheck: true, .d.ts is skipped, but babylon-lite has no .d.ts (source TS) — tsc will check those sources too. Could surface hundreds of errors unrelated to me. Better: run tsc with `--noEmit` and see — or just rely on vite build + runtime.\n\nActually the most valuable checks are: (1) vite build catches import/resolve errors; (2) runtime in browser — not available (user cancelled browser download). So: run vite build, review carefully, restart dev server so user can play.\n\nOne concern about the build: `file:` — no longer a dependency; node_modules/babylon-lite is a manual symlink — vite build should handle it (esbuild resolution follows the symlink; the package's deps resolve via its own node_modules in the reference repo — but wait, in BUILD mode Vite bundles everything; resolving bare imports like \"text-shaper\" from the real package directory — Vite's resolver walks up from the real path → finds ~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite/packages/babylon-lite/node_modules/text-shaper ✓ (confirmed it exists there).\n\nBut do I import text-shaper or recast in my game? No. But index.ts re-exports navigation (recast) and text (text-shaper) modules — in build, esbuild/rollup will include all of index.ts's exports and their deps (rollup bundles the entry graph: main.ts imports specific names from \"babylon-lite\" → index.ts → its static imports pull in all modules including navigation/text). Rollup tree-shakes unused exports if sideEffects: false (babylon-lite's package.json has sideEffects: false ✓). So unused modules get shaken out, and their deps aren't bundled.\n\nOK let's run the build.\n","seq":14706,"t":8199074,"text":"\n\nVerifying the full bundle compiles:\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":121344,"draft_n":1813,"draft_n_accepted":371,"predicted_ms":16010.000000000002,"predicted_n":630,"prompt_ms":3710.0,"prompt_n":1675},"to_request":14462}
