{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Wait — but `createMeshFromData` passes indices to the GPU for rendering. The winding order (front/back face) affects culling. WebGPU's default front face is CCW (counterclockwise) in screen space. If the winding is wrong, the triangles get culled and the terrain becomes invisible!\n\nHmm. What winding does the engine's renderer expect? The engine's own geometry factories (createGround, etc.) use a specific winding, and computeNormals (BJS-style (p1-p2)×(p3-p2)) generates normals consistent with that winding. Since I'm now using a different normal formula, I've reversed the winding relative to what the engine expects for culling.\n\nLet me check the winding of the engine's createGround to know the expected front-face orientation.\n","seq":15170,"t":8271764,"text":"\n\nThe winding also controls culling — let me check the engine's own ground factory to match its front-face convention:\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":127488,"draft_n":791,"draft_n_accepted":217,"predicted_ms":7130.0,"predicted_n":330,"prompt_ms":3490.0,"prompt_n":1854},"to_request":15087}
