{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"The engine's ground uses BJS's winding: triangles (bottomLeft, bottomRight, topRight) and (bottomLeft, bottomRight, topLeft) — that is, in grid coordinates (x → right, z → top... let me try mapping: BJS's ground: is x to the right, z downward? BJS's CreateGround generates in the XZ plane. bottomLeft=(0,0), bottomRight=(1,0), topLeft=(0,1), topRight=(1,1) — with \"top\" meaning +z.\n\nBJS's triangles: (BL, BR, TR) = (a, b, d) and (BL, BR, TL) = (a, b, c). This is exactly the original template I wrote: [a, b, d... no wait: indices are bottomLeft, bottomRight, topRight → a, b, d; then bottomLeft, bottomRight, topLeft → a, b, c.\n\nHmm, BJS's order: [a, b, d, a, b, c]. And BJS's computeNormals ((p1-p2)×(p3-p2)) generates upward normals for that winding (verified earlier: (a,b,c) → up under the BJS formula).\n\nSo the engine's convention is:\n- Winding: [a, b, d, a, b, c] (upward-facing)\n- Normals: BJS formula (p1-p2)×(p3-p2)\n\nBoth must be consistent for culling + lighting. My options:\nA. Use the engine's winding [a, b, d, a, b, c] + the BJS-style normal formula (p1-p2)×(p3-p2).\nB. Use my winding [a, c, b, c, d, b] + my formula — culling: the engine culls according to WebGPU's default CCW front face; if the engine's own geometry uses winding A and displays correctly, then winding B (reversed) will be culled.\n\nTherefore, I have to use the engine's winding A together with the BJS-style normals. Let me revert the index template to [a, b, d, a, b, c]... wait, in the file I wrote [a, b, c, b, d, c] = (a,b,c),(b,d,c). BJS is (a,b,d),(a,b,c). Are these equivalent triangles? (a,b,c) is common to both. The second: (b,d,c) vs (a,b,d) — no, different triangles! My original template (a,b,c)+(b,d,c) tiles the cell correctly (two triangles covering the quad). BJS's (a,b,d)+(a,b,c) also tiles the quad. Both are valid tilings; BJS's shares the diagonal a-b... (a,b,d) covers the diagonal b-d? Vertices of triangle (a,b,d)