{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"Build succeeded. The bundle is small (59.7 kB main + dynamic chunks — consistent with Lite's tree-shaking goal).\n\nNext, restart the dev server on port 5180 (was stopped earlier) and do a final code review of the tricky spots:\n\n1. `bots.ts` — `updateBots` signature: (bots, player, playerInvulnerable, terrain, crates, scene, dt, onPlayerHit). In main.ts it's called with player.dead || invuln as the third argument ✓.\n\n2. `bots.ts` — `respawnBot(bot, terrain, i)` is called in spawnBots before `addToScene` — no problem. Inside `updateBots`, `respawnBot(b, terrain, bots.indexOf(b))` — indexOf inside the loop is O(n²) but n=4 so no problem.\n\n3. Bot aim: `tca > 0 && d2 < 0.25` — tca is the projection of (bot−player) onto the direction… wait: cx = b.x - p.x (bot relative to player), tca = c·n. When the ray from the bot passes through the player's sphere: the closest point on the ray to the player center is origin + tca*n, where origin is the bot's position… let me redo: ray o + t*n. Distance from player p: |o - p + t n|². Minimized at t* = (p-o)·n = -tca (since c = o - p). t* must be > 0 → -tca > 0 → tca < 0. I wrote `tca > 0` — the sign is wrong!\n\nCheck: c = o - p (bot minus player). d² = |c + t n|². Minimum at t* = -c·n = -tca. For a hit in front, we need t* > 0 → tca < 0. And d2 = |c|² - (c·n)² is the minimum squared distance ✓ (that part is correct). So the condition should be `tca < 0 && d2 < 0.25`. Let me fix it.\n\n4. Player firing at bot: `botAabb` returns center (b.x, b.y - BOT_EYE + 1.1, b.z), half-extents (0.5, 1.3, 0.5). Bot body: center y is feet+0.8, half-height 0.8 → spans feet..feet+1.6. Head: center feet+1.9, half 0.275 → spans feet+1.625..feet+2.175. Overall: feet..feet+2.175. botAabb center = feet + 1.1, half-height 1.3 → spans feet-0.2..feet+2.4. Close enough (slightly generous box) ✓. Here feet = b.y - BOT_EYE ✓.\n\n5. `killBot` uses `setMeshVisible` + `removeFromScene` — setMeshVisible then removeFromScene is redundant but harmless. Actually, if we're removing from the scene, setMeshVisible is unnecessary. But no problem (belt and suspenders). Hmm — does removeFromScene properly clean up renderables? The feature docs say \"Dispose / Cleanup ✅ Full GPU resource cleanup on dispose\". removeFromScene should handle it. OK.\n\n6. Shadow casters: bots are not included in the shadow casters (only crates) — bot shadows don't appear. Minor visual issue; leave it (or add bot meshes to casters — but they get removed/re-added on death/respawn, requiring re-calling setShadowTaskCasterMeshes. Skip — ESM shadows from crates are enough).\n\n7. In `hasLOS`, the terrain raycast from the bot's eye to the player: `hit.dist >= dist - 0.5` → LOS is clear. ✓\n\n8. `updateBots` — dead bots: `continue` before ground snap ✓.\n\n9. `main.ts` — `input.fire` is only set when locked (controls.ts: fire = fireHeld && locked) ✓.\n\n10. `controls.ts` — Space key: `keys.has(\"Space\")` → jump. In Browsers, Space also scrolls the page — the page has overflow hidden; no problem. Also, Space during pointer lock is fine.\n\n11. Player firing at their own… — no problem.\n\n12. `weapon.ts` — imports `botAabb, killBot` from bots.ts; bots.ts imports `rayAabb` from weapon.ts — circular. In the bundle, rollup handles ESM circulars if there's no TDZ issue at module init time. Module init: bots.ts's top level only defines functions; weapon.ts's top level defines functions. No top-level execution that references the other side. ✓ (The build already succeeded, which proves rollup accepted it.)\n\n13. `terrain.ts` raycast: `if (oy <= sampleHeight(ox, oz)) return null;` — the player's eye is above the ground ✓. Bot eyes are also above the ground ✓.\n\n14. `main.ts` — the player's death overlay is hidden when locked… `overlayEl.classList.toggle(\"hidden\", input.locked || player.dead)` ✓, and the death element is shown when dead ✓.\n\n15. Gun view model: parented to the camera — the engine handles child elements (FreeCamera tags child elements for push invalidation). It should follow.\n\n16. Fog + dark sky ✓.\n\n17. `index.html` — the crosshair span is centered… no problem.\n\nOne more consideration — performance: bot update calls `hasLOS` per bot per frame → terrain.raycast (up to 30/0.25 = 120 samples + bisection only on hit; the LOS raycast stops at dist < 30 → at most 120 iterations, each with a bilinear sample — cheap). Plus a terrain raycast on each bot shot. No problem.\n\nCrater carving: `updateMeshPositions` writes the buffer per frame — GPU upload of 4 chunks × 3.5KB — no problem.\n\nFix the bot aim sign bug, and also double-check the player's `tryFire` bot loop: `t < MAX` ✓.\n\nAlso in `bots.ts` — unused import `setMeshVisible`? No, it's used in killBot. OK.\n\nOne more: `bots.ts` imports `rayAabb` from \"./weapon\" — weapon.ts also imports from \"./bots\" — already verified it's fine.\n\nAlso `main.ts` — `EYE_HEIGHT` is imported and used for respawn ✓.\n\nFix the aim sign.\n","seq":16379,"t":8388383,"text":"\n\nBuild passes — 59.7 kB main chunk, nicely tree-shaken. I spotted a sign bug in the bot aim math (ray-to-sphere test):\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":133888,"draft_n":4452,"draft_n_accepted":1222,"predicted_ms":41180.0,"predicted_n":1858,"prompt_ms":2250.0,"prompt_n":1069},"to_request":15802}
