{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# quake-lite\\n\\nA Quake-style FPS on **Babylon-Lite** (WebGPU-only engine): a noise-heightfield arena where every shot carves a crater, destructible crates, and four bots that wander, take cover-line-of-sight shots at you, and dig up the arena behind you.\\n\\n## Run\\n\\n```bash\\npnpm install   # postinstall symlinks node_modules/babylon-lite to the local engine source\\npnpm dev       # http://localhost:5180\\n```\\n\\n- `babylon-lite` is not a registry dep — `postinstall` symlinks it to `~/git/reference/Babylon/Babylon-Lite/packages/babylon-lite` (TS source, served directly by Vite; see `optimizeDeps.exclude` in `vite.config.ts`).\\n- Requires a WebGPU browser (Chrome/Edge 113+). Click the canvas to pointer-lock.\\n\\n## Controls\\n\\nWASD move · mouse aim · LMB fire · Space jump · Shift sprint · R reload · ESC release mouse.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nNoise terrain and bots are done. Multiplayer is next: the sim is already shaped for it — all game state (`Player`, `Bot`, `Crate`, `Weapon`, `Terrain.heights`) is plain data updated by standalone functions in `onBeforeRender`, with no DOM access except the HUD step in `src/main.ts`. A server would own `player.ts`/`bots.ts`/`weapon.ts`/`terrain.ts` verbatim and ship state deltas; rendering stays client-side.\\n\\n## Layout\\n\\n| File | Role |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `src/terrain.ts` | 128×128 heightfield, 64 chunks; `carveCrater` rewrites heights and re-uploads only affected chunks via `updateMeshPositions`/`updateMeshNormals`; bilinear `sampleHeight`; marching+bisection `raycast` |\\n| `src/player.ts` | Eye-height character controller: gravity, jump, ground snap on the heightfield, soft map bounds |\\n| `src/weapon.ts` | Hitscan from the eye: nearest of bot AABB / crate AABB / terrain ray; 20-round clip, reload |\\n| `src/bots.ts` | Wander/combat state machine, LOS through terrain+crates, distance-scaled aim error, 5 s respawn |\\n| `src/controls.ts` | Pointer lock + keyboard → `FrameInput` |\\n| `src/main.ts` | Engine/scene setup, frame loop, HUD, `window.__quake` test handle |\\n\\n## Test hook\\n\\n`window.__quake` exposes `{ player, weapon, terrain, crates, bots, fire(), move(dx, dz) }` for scripted checks (fires without pointer lock, moves the player).\", \"path\": \"/scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/README.md\"}","id":"call_dc454929f23040998ce13d11","kind":"tool_call","name":"write","outcome":"ran","request":16381,"seq":16429,"shown":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: /scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/README.md.","t":8411192,"turn":4}
