{"kind":"delta","request":16957,"seq":17273,"t":8532931,"tool_call":{"arguments":"{\"file_path\": \"/scratch/run3/babylon-lite-minecraft-fps/src/weapon.ts\", \"new_string\": \"export function rayAabb(\\n    ox: number,\\n    oy: number,\\n    oz: number,\\n    dx: number,\\n    dy: number,\\n    dz: number,\\n    cx: number,\\n    cy: number,\\n    cz: number,\\n    hx: number,\\n    hy: number,\\n    hz: number\\n): number | null {\\n    let tmin = 0;\\n    let tmax = Infinity;\\n    const os = [ox, oy, oz];\\n    const cs = [cx, cy, cz];\\n    const ds = [dx, dy, dz];\\n    const hs = [hx, hy, hz];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n        if (Math.abs(ds[i]!) < 1e-8) {\\n            if (os[i]! - cs[i]! < -hs[i]! || os[i]! - cs[i]! > hs[i]!) return null;\\n        } else {\\n            let t1 = (cs[i]! - hs[i]! - os[i]!) / ds[i]!;\\n            let t2 = (cs[i]! + hs[i]! - os[i]!) / ds[i]!;\\n            if (t1 > t2) {\\n                const t = t1;\\n                t1 = t2;\\n                t2 = t;\\n            }\\n            tmin = Math.max(tmin, t1);\\n            tmax = Math.min(tmax, t2);\\n            if (tmin > tmax) return null;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    return tmin;\\n}\", \"old_string\": \"export function rayAabb(\\n    ox: number,\\n    oy: number,\\n    oz: number,\\n    dx: number,\\n    dy: number,\\n    dz: number,\\n    cx: number,\\n    cy: number,\\n    cz: number,\\n    half: number\\n): number | null {\\n    let tmin = 0;\\n    let tmax = Infinity;\\n    const os = [ox, oy, oz];\\n    const cs = [cx, cy, cz];\\n    const ds = [dx, dy, dz];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\\n        if (Math.abs(ds[i]!) < 1e-8) {\\n            if (os[i]! - cs[i]! < -half || os[i]! - cs[i]! > half) return null;\\n        } else {\\n            let t1 = (cs[i]! - half - os[i]!) / ds[i]!;\\n            let t2 = (cs[i]! + half - os[i]!) / ds[i]!;\\n            if (t1 > t2) {\\n                const t = t1;\\n                t1 = t2;\\n                t2 = t;\\n            }\\n            tmin = Math.max(tmin, t1);\\n            tmax = Math.min(tmax, t2);\\n            if (tmin > tmax) return null;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    return tmin;\\n}\"}","id":"call_ba5fbf0e8ebf42fdaa4bb202","index":0,"name":"edit"}}
{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","kind":"response","reasoning":"main.ts looks consistent. Remaining concerns:\n\n1. **Gun view model is parented to the camera** — risk: if the engine's default render task doesn't draw camera-parented meshes, the gun will disappear. I confirmed earlier that FreeCamera explicitly tags children for push invalidation, which suggests that parented children are supported. If it doesn't render, the user just won't see the gun — a minor visual issue, and the rest of the game will work. Acceptable risk. I'll mention it in the summary.\n\n2. **Bot spawn positions**: `respawnBot` uses `index/4 * 2π` — 4 bots at fixed quadrants + jitter ✓.\n\n3. **Bots walking over crater edges**: the ground snap teleports them down 2–3 units — a bit floaty but acceptable.\n\n4. **`updateBots` while the player is dead**: bots keep wandering (canSee = false) ✓.\n\n5. **Bot LOS against its own… no problem.**\n\n6. **The `weapon.ts` crate list passed to `setShadowTaskCasterMeshes`** — after a crate is destroyed, the remaining casters get updated ✓. Bots are not casters (already noted).\n\n7. **`index.html`** — the overlay's initial text says \"CLICK TO PLAY\" — good.\n\n8. **TypeScript strict mode**: I'm not running tsc. Rollup's build succeeded (esbuild strips types without checking). There may be type errors (e.g., `mesh.material = null as unknown` in createMeshFromData — the engine's own code). My code: `botAabb` returns an object — used with spread? No, field access ✓. `rayAabb(p.x, p.y, p.z, dx, dy, dz, a.cx, a.cy, a.cz, a.hx, a.hy, a.hz)` — 10 args ✓ matches the signature (ox,oy,oz,dx,dy,dz,cx,cy,cz,half) — wait. The signature of rayAabb: (ox, oy, oz, dx, dy, dz, cx, cy, cz, half) — 10 parameters, one `half` (a cube). But I'm passing a.hx, a.hy, a.hz — 11 args! Let me check weapon.ts's rayAabb — it's a cube-only AABB!\n\nLooking at the original rayAabb in weapon.ts:\n```ts\nexport function rayAabb(ox, oy, oz, dx, dy, dz, cx, cy, cz, half): number | null {\n    ... os/cs/ds arrays, per-axis half is the same value ...\n```\nYes — a single `half` for all axes (cube). But in the bot hit test I'm calling it with (a.cx, a.cy, a.cz, a.hx, a.hy, a.hz) — 11 args. TypeScript would flag this, but esbuild doesn't. At runtime: the extra argument `a.hz` is ignored, and `half = a.hx` (0.5) is used for all axes — so the bot's hitbox becomes a cube of radius 0.5 centered at (x, y-0.4, z) — the bot's actual height is about 2.2. The player would need to aim at the mid-chest box — gameplay-wise it's kind of OK (a narrower target), but the hy=1.3 parameter I designed is unused.\n\nFix: make rayAabb support per-axis half-extents (hx, hy, hz) — cleaner, and use it correctly for both crates (hx=hy=hz=size/2) and bots.\n\nLet me update the signature of rayAabb in weapon.ts to (ox,oy,oz,dx,dy,dz,cx,cy,cz,hx,hy,hz), and update the crate call sites to pass c.size/2 three times.\n","seq":17274,"t":8532931,"text":"\n\nFound a real bug: `rayAabb` only accepts a single cube `half`, but the bot hitbox call passes three half-extents (11 args — the extras are silently ignored). Making it per-axis:\n\n","timings":{"cache_n":140032,"draft_n":3220,"draft_n_accepted":1279,"predicted_ms":30650.0,"predicted_n":1739,"prompt_ms":6010.0,"prompt_n":2903},"to_request":16957}
