{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"5183 is serving the latest code.\n\nSummary of the situation:\n- Project: `quake-lite` inside the session's working directory (the scratchpad mirroring the worktree — since the worktree root is outside my writable sandbox, I couldn't move it directly. The user can `cp -R` it to the worktree).\n- The dev server on 5183 is serving the latest build. 5180/5182 are old, sandbox-locked duplicates, and the user can kill them (pids 65476, 77191) to free up 5180.\n- Scope achieved: noise terrain ✓ (already built previously), bots ✓ (4 of them, wandering/combat/LOS/aim error/respawn), player health + death/respawn ✓, crates ✓, multiplayer: deferred, but the simulation is in a plain-data shape that's easy to port to a server.\n- Verified: production build ✓, tsc clean across the whole program ✓ (including engine sources), module graph ✓. Not verified: actual rendering in a browser (the user canceled the Playwright browser download, and there's no browser available here) — so runtime behavior (rendering, shadows, the gun's parent-node rendering) needs a human to open it and check.\n\nWhat to tell the user:\n1. What was built (scope: noise terrain + bots, multiplayer deferred).\n2. Where it lives + how to run it (5183 is the live one; kill the old servers to use 5180).\n3. What was verified vs. what needs a human's eyes.\n4. Key files/functions.\n\nKeep it concise.\n","seq":18535,"t":8701426,"text":"\n\nDone. Here's where things stand:\n\n**What's built** (scope: noise terrain + bots; multiplayer deferred but the sim is server-ready)\n- `src/terrain.ts` — 128×128 noise heightfield in 64 chunks; `carveCrater()` rewrites heights and re-uploads only the affected chunks via `updateMeshPositions`/`updateMeshNormals`; bilinear `sampleHeight()`; marching+bisection `raycast()`.\n- `src/bots.ts` — 4 bots: wander a 38-unit arena, take shots when you're within 30 units with LOS (terrain *and* crates block), distance-scaled aim error, 8–14 dmg/hit, 5 s respawn. They carve the terrain and break crates on misses.\n- `src/player.ts` / `src/weapon.ts` — eye-height character controller (gravity, jump, ground snap); hitscan that resolves nearest of bot AABB / crate AABB / terrain; 20-round clip, auto-reload. Player has 100 HP, death screen, 2 s respawn invulnerability.\n- `src/main.ts` — engine setup, frame loop, Quake-style HUD (health/ammo/crosshair), `window.__quake` test handle.\n\n**Verified**\n- `pnpm build` ✓ (59.7 kB main chunk — tree-shaking is working)\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean across the whole program, including the engine source\n- Fixed two real bugs found in review: bot aim ray-sphere sign error, and `rayAabb` now takes per-axis half-extents (the 11-arg bot call was silently ignored under the old cube signature)\n\n**Needs your eyes** — I couldn't run a browser here (the Playwright download was cancelled, and headless WebGPU needs it), so actual rendering is unverified: whether the camera-parented gun view model draws, shadow behavior, and general look.\n\n**Run it**: the live server is **http://localhost:5183** (fresh, serving current code). The old servers on 5180/5182 are stale and sandbox-locked — kill pids `65476` and `77191` if you want 5180 back.\n\nOne note: the worktree root is outside my writable sandbox (EPERM), so the project lives in the session workdir, not `~/git/me/discipline/.claude/worktrees/react-spa-prototype-e65246/` — `cp -R` it in whenever you like. For multiplayer next: `player.ts`/`bots.ts`/`weapon.ts`/`terrain.ts` are plain-data sim with no DOM, so a server can own them verbatim and ship state deltas.","timings":{"cache_n":150784,"draft_n":2569,"draft_n_accepted":615,"predicted_ms":25100.0,"predicted_n":982,"prompt_ms":1260.0,"prompt_n":367},"to_request":18164}
